! TEMPLATE: Solute Minimization
! DESCRIPTION: Minimize solute atoms while keeping solvent frozen using steepest descent
! TYPE: minimization
! PRIORITY: 3
! AUTHOR: Erika McCarthy, Şölen Ekesan, and Darrin M. York
! VERSION: 1.0
! SOURCE: https://ambertutorials-rutgerslbsr-c744272d5a9c1169e0dc9e19b8d800019105.gitlab.io/workshop/02_intoMD/MTR1/Build_MTR1.html

Solute energy minimization. Restraints on the solute are released to relax the solute and solvent with respect to each other and alleviate potential clashes present from the crystal. This will not dramatically impact the solute structure.

&cntrl
! Run Control
  imin = 1,			! Energy minimization (0=MD, 1=minimization)
  ntmin = 0,			! Minimization method (0=conjugate gradient after ncyc steepest descent)
  maxcyc = 2000,		! Maximum minimization cycles

! Input_Output Control
  ntx = 1,			! Read coordinates and/or velocities: 1 = start, 5 = restart
  ntpr = 0,			! Every ntpr steps, print human-readable energy info
  ntwx = 0,			! Every ntwx steps, print coordinates to mdcrd file

! Restraints
  ntr = 1,				! Enable positional restraints (see restraintmask below)
  restraint_wt = 0.0,			! Restraint force constant (kcal/mol-A2)
  restraintmask = '!@H= & !:WAT,Na+,Cl-,K+,MG', ! Atoms to restrain (AMBER mask syntax)


! Miscellaneous
  cut = 12.0,			! Nonbonded interaction cutoff (Angstroms)
/
